CloudBurrow patch 11 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bugs: #1109, #1121).

The bug: googlesqlite hands a SQL NULL to a function as a nil value.Value,
and these functions called a method on it without looking, so the call
panicked, nothing recovered it, and the BigQuery emulator answered the query
500 (which the official clients retry): ARRAY_TO_STRING, ARRAY_CONCAT,
ARRAY_REVERSE, NET.IP_TO_STRING, NET.IP_TRUNC, NET.IPV4_FROM_INT64,
NET.IPV4_TO_INT64, NET.PUBLIC_SUFFIX, NET.REG_DOMAIN, the step of
GENERATE_DATE_ARRAY and GENERATE_TIMESTAMP_ARRAY, MAKE_INTERVAL, INTERVAL
<NULL> <part>, ST_BUFFER, ST_BUFFERWITHTOLERANCE, ST_INTERSECTSBOX,
NULLIF(x, NULL), JSON_OBJECT's key and JSON_SET's path and value (found by
calling every registered function with a nil argument). ST_DISTANCE,
ST_HAUSDORFFDWITHIN, JUSTIFY_DAYS, JUSTIFY_HOURS, JUSTIFY_INTERVAL and
JSON_TYPE returned an error; and IN and IN UNNEST returned FALSE where a
comparison with NULL decides. In BigQuery "If an operand is NULL, the
function result is NULL" unless the function says otherwise (function call
rules), ARRAY_CONCAT "returns NULL if any input argument is NULL", the
GENERATE_*_ARRAY functions return "a NULL array" if any argument is NULL,
"If json_key is NULL, an error is produced" (JSON_OBJECT), and IN returns
FALSE for an empty set, TRUE for a match, NULL if a comparison with NULL
decides, FALSE otherwise. The patch, in the one place every scalar
function is called from (setupNormalFuncMap), returns NULL for a NULL
argument of the functions above without calling them, and returns any
function's panic as an error naming it; and fixes JSON_OBJECT, JSON_SET,
NULLIF, IN and IN UNNEST. null_arguments_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it; the module's own array bind_test.go, which held
NULL IN UNNEST([1]) FALSE, now holds it NULL.

